WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm sorry
about that stumble.

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let me explain.
-Did you stumble?

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
I staggered a little bit.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.839 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It is not alcohol.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:08.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm...
[ Audience laughs ]

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:10.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Some doubt!
Some doubt from the audience!

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Let's just talk
between ourselves.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.547 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I have vertigo.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Forever?
-Even on your studio set.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've had it about five months,
and it is diminishing.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am told it will go away
in time.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
That explains
my little tottering there

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a moment.
It was not alcohol!

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience laughs ]
-Well, thank you

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.063
for fighting through that
and being here, because this is

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.899
very exciting.
-Nobody else I would do it for.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:33.700 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Well, I appreciate it.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.202
Although, I'm pretty sure
I've seen you on talk shows

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:41.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
all week long.
[ Audience laughs ]

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.742 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Found out!

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
Darn!
-Still, I mean, Patrick,

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:46.613
you have a long,
you have an illustrious career.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
Royal Shakespeare Company
for ten years.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah!
-But here you are,

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Poop Emoji.
Was this...

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know, I know.
-Was it all --

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:55.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel like
it was all heading for this?

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:58.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do that again!
-Was it all heading for this?

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Isn't that wonderful?
Um..

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you play that
in reverse, it's...

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:04.330 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:09.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I always knew that there was
something waiting for me.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:16.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's very hard
to talk seriously about

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
this role, you know.
-Yeah.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But this must --
I mean, again, of the Emojis,

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
this must've been
a coveted role.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:26.352
I would feel like many actors
would've said yes right away

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the Poop Emoji.
Did you have to fight for this

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:29.656 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of the Emojis?

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fight other actors?
-Yeah!

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no, no.
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:36.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um, it came to me,
and it came in an e-mail.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:40.567
And it was the quickest response
I have ever given to any...

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You jumped for it.
-Jumped all over it!

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes, exclamation mark,
exclamation mark.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:50.210
-Well, I think it's a gift,
because now I will never be able

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
to separate the Poop Emoji
from your voice.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.348 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:58.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that will give it
a great dignity.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is that going to be
a problem for you, Seth?

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.654 size:88% position:44%
-I don't know, I don't.
I think it'll make be --

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
It'll make my life better.
What happened there?

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Excuse me, I don't know.
I've got threads hanging out

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.894 size:81% position:41% line:92%
of my shirt, you know?

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.262 size:78% position:39%
-Believe it or not...
-I've got to stop..

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...I think if
you'd have left it alone,

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:16.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
we wouldn't have noticed.
[ Audience laughs ]

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.871 line:92%
-You know, I am a great fan.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've talked about
your early work as well

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:23.176
when you've been here
in the past, because even before

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Star Trek," I knew you
from some BBC productions.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:29.149
And I was looking back,
and I actually found on YouTube

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.984 line:92%
you playing Horatio in "Hamlet."

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is young
Patrick Stewart.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:37.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, that is just fantastic.
[ Audience cheers ]

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:41.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Now, that's a wig?

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.362 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience laughs ]

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, a wig!
Is it a wig!

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, what did
you think I said?

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.334 size:81% position:41%
-[ Laughs ] I thought
you said, "Is it win?"

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:52.405
And I was...
-Is it a win to do Shakespeare?

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a hairpiece.
-Oh, it's a hairpiece.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.308 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's too little of it
to be a wig.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:59.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the secret
of wearing false hair.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:03.383
You wear as little as possible,
then it looks more natural.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:03.950 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, gotcha.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You will not have
to worry about that

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.121 line:92%
for a very, very long time.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this, by the way,
I have to say,

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
is an actor called
Ian Richardson.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ian Richardson's
a fantastic actor.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great and brilliant actor.
-Yeah.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, we talked about
"Tinker Tailor Soldier Spy"

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you were in it.
He was Bill Haydon in that,

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was one of
the great roles.

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wonderful performance.
-Yeah, absolutely.

